  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "These are also proverbs of Solomon, which the men of Hezekiah king of Judah copied out.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "It is the glory of God to conceal a thing: but the honour of kings is to search out a matter.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "The heaven for height, and the earth for depth, and the heart of kings is unsearchable.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Take away the dross from the silver, and there shall come forth a vessel for the finer.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Take away the wicked from before the king, and his throne shall be established in righteousness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Put not forth thyself in the presence of the king, and stand not in the place of great men:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "For better it is that it be said unto thee, Come up hither; than that thou shouldest be put lower in the presence of the prince whom thine eyes have seen.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Go not forth hastily to strive, lest thou know not what to do in the end thereof, when thy neighbour hath put thee to shame.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Debate thy cause with thy neighbour himself; and discover not a secret to another:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Lest he that heareth it put thee to shame, and thine infamy turn not away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "A word fitly spoken is like apples of gold in pictures of silver.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "As an earring of gold, and an ornament of fine gold, so is a wise reprover upon an obedient ear.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "As the cold of snow in the time of harvest, so is a faithful messenger to them that send him: for he refresheth the soul of his masters.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Whoso boasteth himself of a false gift is like clouds and wind without rain.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "By long forbearing is a prince persuaded, and a soft tongue breaketh the bone.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Hast thou found honey? eat so much as is sufficient for thee, lest thou be filled therewith, and vomit it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Withdraw thy foot from thy neighbour’s house; lest he be weary of thee, and so hate thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "A man that beareth false witness against his neighbour is a maul, and a sword, and a sharp arrow.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Confidence in an unfaithful man in time of trouble is like a broken tooth, and a foot out of joint.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "As he that taketh away a garment in cold weather, and as vinegar upon nitre, so is he that singeth songs to an heavy heart.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "If thine enemy be hungry, give him bread to eat; and if he be thirsty, give him water to drink:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "For thou shalt heap coals of fire upon his head, and the LORD shall reward thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "The north wind driveth away rain: so doth an angry countenance a backbiting tongue.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "It is better to dwell in the corner of the housetop, than with a brawling woman and in a wide house.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "As cold waters to a thirsty soul, so is good news from a far country.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "A righteous man falling down before the wicked is as a troubled fountain, and a corrupt spring.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "It is not good to eat much honey: so for men to search their own glory is not glory.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:25:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "He that hath no rule over his own spirit is like a city that is broken down, and without walls.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 25:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:25:28"
      }
    }
  ],
